        "section": "textiles",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Pattern Making",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "THREE ROUTES TO A PATTERN:\n  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n  │  FLAT PATTERN DRAFTING                                       │\n  │  Mathematical construction from measurements                 │\n  │  Tools: rulers, French curves, set squares                   │\n  │  Starting point: sloper (basic block, minimum ease)          │\n  │  Reproducible, scalable, industrial standard                 │\n  ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n  │  DRAPING (MOULAGE)                                           │\n  │  Fabric draped and pinned on dress form                      │\n  │  Marks transferred to paper                                  │\n  │  Intuitive for complex 3D shapes (cowls, bias)               │\n  │  Couture standard; reveals how fabric \"wants\" to behave      │\n  ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n  │  COMMERCIAL PATTERN ADJUSTMENT                               │\n  │  Start from existing commercial pattern                      │\n  │  Baste toile → fit → adjust → re-cut                         │\n  │  Common for home sewers                                      │\n  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```"
    },
